# Copy to .env.local to change modes. NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are inlined at BUILD time: restart `npm run dev` / rebuild after changing.
# A PRODUCTION build (`npm run build`) refuses to run unless NEXT_PUBLIC_USE_MOCK is set to true or false, and in real mode
# (false) unless NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL and NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL are real public addresses, not localhost.
# Launch build: also set LAUNCH_BUILD=true (build-time only) to refuse a placeholder WhatsApp number.

# ── Mode 1: mock (default) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# No API needed. Data lives in the browser (localStorage "fbf-mock-v1"); logins maya@example.com / admin@fuzzball.test, password fuzzball123.
# `npm run dev` runs mock when the variable is unset; a production build needs it set explicitly to "true".
# NEXT_PUBLIC_USE_MOCK=true

# ── Mode 2: real NestJS API (../api) ───────────────────────────────────
# 1. cd ../api && npm run seed && npm run start:dev   (http://localhost:4000, same seeded logins, password fuzzball123)
# 2. api/.env WEB_ORIGIN must include this app's origin, e.g. WEB_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000 (comma-separated for several).
#    Cookies are SameSite=Lax, so web and API must be the same *site* (localhost:3000 <-> localhost:4000 is fine).
# 3. Uncomment:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_USE_MOCK=false
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4000
#
# Online payments: with no RAZORPAY_* keys the API is in mock payment mode and the "Test payment" modals work end to end.
# With real Razorpay keys the checkout needs the Razorpay window (TODO seam in src/lib/api/http.ts `settlePayment`).

# Optional
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WHATSAPP=910000000000
# Build-time: the maker's Cloudinary cloud name, so Next's image optimiser only accepts that account's pictures.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CLOUDINARY_CLOUD=
# International shipping is off at launch (India only): checkout, the delivery check and all shipping copy offer India
# alone. Set to true once Razorpay international payments and export invoices are in place (TODOS.md).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SHIPS_INTERNATIONAL=false
